{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness","id":907001,"title":"Shadowlands and the Wilderness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-03T23:32:05-07:00","id":907001,"title":"Shadowlands and the Wilderness","content":"Okay one big thing I reckon we have been missing is more Wraith material on what its like in the Shadowlands of the Wilderness. Like Forests, Jungles, the Desert. Its ripe virgin territory for spooky story ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:31:13-07:00","id":907016,"title":"","content":"It's the Tempest.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it is. I thought I had answered this in a previous thread, but looking through the catalogue, I guess I never posted it. Think of the Shadowlands as a fine gauze that blankets the &quot;real&quot; world - and necropolis are like &quot;psychic weights&quot; that pin down and conform to the Skinlands surrounding them. Any unexplored/uninhabited areas are the Tempest. There may be Byways connecting Necropoli reflecting highways connecting cities, but the Underworld is not a 1:1 analogue. Anything that is not &quot;settled&quot; or &quot;civilized&quot; is the Tempest.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T05:30:58-07:00","id":907065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907016#post907016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Tempest.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it is. I thought I had answered this in a previous thread, but looking through the catalogue, I guess I never posted it. Think of the Shadowlands as a fine gauze that blankets the &quot;real&quot; world - and necropolis are like &quot;psychic weights&quot; that pin down and conform to the Skinlands surrounding them. Any unexplored/uninhabited areas are the Tempest. There may be Byways connecting Necropoli reflecting highways connecting cities, but the Underworld is not a 1:1 analogue. Anything that is not &quot;settled&quot; or &quot;civilized&quot; is the Tempest.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> I was always under the impression that the Shadowlands pretty faithfully corresponded to the Skinlands, differing primarily in look and substance.<br /> <br /> Wraiths battling during the Great War were often out in the sticks. Unless such places sprang into being because of emotional investment I was of the opinion they already existed.<br /> Think of the Somme: were Wraiths unable to venture there before the war?<br /> I've never seen Necropoli existing as islands in a storm.<br /> The Dark Kingdoms and Far Shores yes, but I thought the Shadowlands existed as a separate plane from the Tempest.<br /> <br /> Please correct me if I'm wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":1309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","user":"Andreas Rayne","date":". 06-04-2016, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:47:40-07:00","id":907139,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1309\" data-vbnamecard=\"1309\">Andreas Rayne</a> Forgive me, I wasn't exactly clear. It was late and I was tired. These &quot;uncivilized&quot; and unsettled areas are more &quot;Tempest-lite&quot; than &quot;proper&quot; Sea of Shadows. A field may shift and roil, being covered in tall grass one moment, a muddy pit the next. Spectres and Plasmics might roam, and sudden Nihils fissure open. There just isn't enough emotional investment or psychic weight to &quot;stabilize&quot; those areas. Most uninhabited areas are reflective of their Skinlands counterparts, but more representative than analogous. So a forest in the Shadowlands may occupy the same space as a forest in the Skinlands, but not every tree will share the exact same placement (and the Shadowlands forest will vary in appearance and mood depending on what the Wraiths expect).<br /> <br /> Necropoli are more like islands in a calm sea rather than a storm, so calm that it's often mistaken for land. A Maelstrom will quickly disabuse anyone of that notion, though.<br /> <br /> It's not that Wraiths weren't able to access places like the Somme, but that the Somme wasn't<i> the Somme</i> until it was <b>the Somme</b>, if that makes sense, like Verdun was just some hills until it was <b>Verdun</b>, and the beaches at Normandy were just a place where sand met water until D-Day. The geographical features and emotional resonances weren't &quot;locked in&quot; until those events happened.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:16:50-07:00","id":907153,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I interpret it as a combination of the two. For me, it comes down to not wanting to make any hard and fast HRs about what-is and what-is-not enough emotional investment to give a location a place in the Shadowlands. I\u2019ve used untamed regions as places where Byways coalesce and take wraiths into the Tempest at the speed of plot.<br /> <br /> Back to the OP\u2019s thoughts about \u201cvirgin territory for spooky ideas!\u201d<br /> <br /> If you want to go with the notion that places in the Shadowlands only form with strong emotional investment, I'd go with emotional quality over quantity. Strong and intense emotions that create little pockets of \u201cpsychic weight\u201d (I like that analogy).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Forest: A log cabin shared by two prospectors. They strike it rich, but not before winter sets in. With thoughts displaced by a perfect storm of greed, paranoia, and hunger, one of the partners violently kills the other and throws his body outside. The food still runs out and he dies with the regret of a murderer.</span><br /> The Circle finds this cabin in the neverwhere. It\u2019s a small Haunt inhabited by a lonely wraith who is under constant attack by a rampaging spectre. What does the Circle do when they find out the wraith they\u2019re helping is a killer and the monster outside just wants revenge (or justice)?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Jungle: After some minor conflict during the mid-twentieth century, there\u2019s a patch of jungle littered with the burnt-out and shot-down husks of fighter jets. Not all of the pilots ejected. Some were stuck in their flaming cockpit-coffins as they plummeted to earth, grasping for tattered photos of loved ones. Others took bodily hits by bullets, cursing their hated enemies between teeth soaked with their own blood.</span><br /> The small group of wraiths that call this area home come from different regions of the world. They\u2019re content to spend eternity with the people they fought against, but different Dark Kingdoms are making claims for these souls and this territory. Are characters sent there as liaisons to integrate them into the Hierarchy? Are they sent with slavers\u2019 chains? Or are they Renegades who want to help this small band of restless dead retain their anonymity?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Desert: It made international news! For a few minutes, at least. The headline read \u201cArcheology Students Found Too Late!\u201d A bus of archaeology interns was traveling through the desert on the way to a site. It blew a tire on the road. No big deal. They had a spare. That someone forgot to pack it. That was alright, they had plenty of water. Except they didn\u2019t. Surely they\u2019d be rescued. When the bus doesn\u2019t arrive, the university would coordinate with local authorities to find the missing students, which would have worked if the police weren\u2019t corrupt. By the time the bus was located, everyone was dead from exposure [<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">insert writer joke here</span>].</span><br /> Archeology didn\u2019t pan out, so the \u201csurvivors\u201d are trying their hands at business. Using the bus as their tollbooth, they tax all travelers. Pathos, relics, whatever. Are the characters wanderers that get caught at the tollbooth? Or are they Legionaries sent to bring these miscreants under heal? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:21:46-07:00","id":907161,"title":"","content":"Any sources on that? Because I've never gotten that impression and there is definitely material that directly contradicts it. E.g. Wraiths that venture out of Necropoli in the Western reaches of the US seem to vanish from time to time and might be/are victims of some vengeful Dark Kingdom of Flint remnants. <br /> <br /> I can see it as being more subjective than a real world foot by foot correspondence, but I don't think there's much to indicate that it's just &quot;calm Tempest&quot; with shifting scenery. <br /> <br /> Plus, there is a general tendency to equate Tempest in the &quot;flat&quot; perspective with water, specifically large bodies. In a 3+ D perspective it's also &quot;up&quot; and &quot;down&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:31:24-07:00","id":907166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907153#post907153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Desert: It made international news! For a few minutes, at least. The headline read \u201cArcheology Students Found Too Late!\u201d A bus of archaeology interns was traveling through the desert on the way to a site. It blew a tire on the road. No big deal. They had a spare. That someone forgot to pack it. That was alright, they had plenty of water. Except they didn\u2019t. Surely they\u2019d be rescued. When the bus doesn\u2019t arrive, the university would coordinate with local authorities to find the missing students, which would have worked if the police weren\u2019t corrupt. By the time the bus was located, everyone was dead from exposure [<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">insert writer joke here</span>].</span><br /> Archeology didn\u2019t pan out, so the \u201csurvivors\u201d are trying their hands at business. Using the bus as their tollbooth, they tax all travelers. Pathos, relics, whatever. Are the characters wanderers that get caught at the tollbooth? Or are they Legionaries sent to bring these miscreants under heal? [/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr.... ummm..... No. As an archaeologist, that isn't going to work. A &quot;bus&quot; of archaeologists (not sure what an archaeological intern is) would probably be one of the more capable groups to strand in the wilderness. They will also have plenty of provisions as well as a massive set of skills to manipulate the environment. Want to know how people have found water in a desert prior to Western civilization found water in the desert? Ask the archaeologists. Someone has written a paper on the hydrology of the area and how it has been exploited over time. Another has done a thorough ethnohistory of the area and talked to the remnants of the indigenous population about survival. Problems with shade and heat regulation? Every archaeologist has had to deal with this sort of problem for years as a part of doing business. I've had actual civil engineering interns on archaeological sites and just give up because it's so much harder than working on a crew pushing a new road through the wilderness. <br /> <br /> Maybe a bus of college students? Or a busload of archaeolgists working in the wrong place at the wrong time with regard to local conflict or customs? (I'm reminder strongly of the time we had to spend in our trenches because of the noises of random gunfire. Until the perpetrators walked out of the woods and told us they were out having fun &quot;Shootin' and drinkin' beers&quot;...) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T11:08:11-07:00","id":907194,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> : Thanks for the IRL intel. I'm (obviously) not an archaeologist. It was just a snip I came up with off the top of my head to help the OP get some ideas.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:08:23-07:00","id":907330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907139#post907139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Forgive me, I wasn't exactly clear. It was late and I was tired. These &amp;quot;uncivilized&amp;quot; and unsettled areas are more &amp;quot;Tempest-lite&amp;quot; than &amp;quot;proper&amp;quot; Sea of Shadows. A field may shift and roil, being covered in tall grass one moment, a muddy pit the next. Spectres and Plasmics might roam, and sudden Nihils fissure open. There just isn't enough emotional investment or psychic weight to &amp;quot;stabilize&amp;quot; those areas. Most uninhabited areas are reflective of their Skinlands counterparts, but more representative than analogous. So a forest in the Shadowlands may occupy the same space as a forest in the Skinlands, but not every tree will share the exact same placement (and the Shadowlands forest will vary in appearance and mood depending on what the Wraiths expect).<br /> <br /> Necropoli are more like islands in a calm sea rather than a storm, so calm that it's often mistaken for land. A Maelstrom will quickly disabuse anyone of that notion, though.<br /> <br /> It's not that Wraiths weren't able to access places like the Somme, but that the Somme wasn't<i> the Somme</i> until it was <b>the Somme</b>, if that makes sense, like Verdun was just some hills until it was <b>Verdun</b>, and the beaches at Normandy were just a place where sand met water until D-Day. The geographical features and emotional resonances weren't &amp;quot;locked in&amp;quot; until those events happened.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>This causes all sorts of problems with the Rule of Ouch. Individual trees do have to be in exactly the same place in the Shadowlands as in the Skinlands, or the Rule of Ouch loses meaning.<br /> <br /> Also, bear in mind that most of the world has been traversed by *someone* at some point. I don't buy that it would be Tempest-lite. Wild and more chaotic, yes, but the physical markers would be the same. They would just be surrounded by fog, peppered with nihils and prowled by nasties. But the geography would be otherwise similar to anywhere else in the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:23:43-07:00","id":907334,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">There\u2019s a wide variety of opinions and \u2013 Wr20 notwithstanding \u2013 I don\u2019t think there are any definitive rules on the subject. Go with what you think sounds cool/engaging. If you want a Tempest-lite \u2122 a la <i>Insidious</i>\u2019s the Further, go for it. If you want a hellish nightmare parody of nature, like Clive Barker directing <i>Never Cry Wolf</i>, go for it. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:16:48-07:00","id":907359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907194#post907194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> : Thanks for the IRL intel. I'm (obviously) not an archaeologist. It was just a snip I came up with off the top of my head to help the OP get some ideas.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>There's likely to be someone on that bus that knows how to knap flint....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:28:36-07:00","id":907363,"title":"","content":"I've never considered the &quot;wilderness&quot; of the Shadowlands the same as the Tempest. In fact, I disagree with almost everything that nothing has said. The Tempest was simply the hyperdimensional reality &quot;between&quot; the Shadowlands and Stygia (and other Dark Kingdoms) and Far Shores which was accessible through nihils or argos.<br /> <br /> If you go back far enough time, not only are there no necropoli, there aren't even major cities as we understand them today. Most people live in the rural areas, and most cities are merely the size of small towns.<br /> <br /> Ghost stories can happen anywhere. Ancient battlefields, isolated log cabins where terrible crimes happened, places where people were trapped and starved; all of that is prime territory for hauntings.<br /> <br /> Wraith can do stories in the wilderness just like it can anywhere else. It's just that the Hierarchy is far away - any sort of legionnaries would be placed under the control of a Regent (a glorified marshal) who is appointed by a local Necropolis to administer that territory. These legionnaires are probably located in the most powerful Haunt of a local area where they can patrol the entire territory. They'd mainly be interested in populated areas so they can oversee the reaping and governance of the dead, so it would be very infrequent to send a patrol out in the real wilderness. Much more likely would be freewraiths eeking out an existence on their own, or perhaps a small group of Heretics or Renegades hiding out.<br /> <br /> Wraiths require Passions, so they need people to harvest them from. So the wilderness is dangerous - many wraiths will run out of Pathos - unless they can find someone out there who has very strong emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T21:22:45-07:00","id":907436,"title":"","content":"Wow. Okay. I step away for a day... Allow me to clarify: When I said &quot;Tempest-lite,&quot; I meant it was similar to the Tempest, not part of the actual Tempest. Unsettled wilderness areas are akin to the foam on a latte, where the coffee itself is the Tempest. Nihils would be holes in the foam, and when a Maelstrom comes along, it shakes the whole cup. Things don't change instantly either, I meant that a field of tall grass might become a muddy pit when a character crests a hill rather than blinks their eyes.<br /> <br /> As for where this information comes from, I extrapolated from 1st &amp; 2nd edition, several pieces of fiction<sup>\u2020</sup> from various books, scenes in the novels <i>Caravan of Shadows</i> and <i>Beyond the Shroud</i>, and <i>Ghost Towns</i> (which probably has the most information on wilderness/lightly settled areas). The closest there's been on an official ruling is in the <i>Player's Guide</i>, from in in-character journal entry, which says the Shadowlands are <u>almost</u> an exact replica of the Skinlands. So a desert in the Shadowlands occupies the same &quot;space&quot; as a desert in the Skinlands, but unless something happened there (or there are Nihils around), it's just kind of &quot;generic desert&quot; - there's no psychic imprint to give the place unique features (unless they is a unique feature already found there, like the sandstone pillars in Utah, which people travel to see, thus leaving a psychic/emotional tag).<br /> <br /> This is all just what I've pieced together, though, so take it with a grain of salt. Wild areas are more &quot;soft&quot; and mutable than the areas around a Necropolis, especially if there's a Nihil nearby, but still reflective of their Skinlands counterparts.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> <sup>\u2020(If this were the <i>Vampire</i> forums, I'm sure the first response would be something like &quot;You can't use the fiction to answer a question!&quot;)</sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 06-05-2016, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T03:16:41-07:00","id":907552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907139#post907139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Forgive me, I wasn't exactly clear. It was late and I was tired. These &amp;quot;uncivilized&amp;quot; and unsettled areas are more &amp;quot;Tempest-lite&amp;quot; than &amp;quot;proper&amp;quot; Sea of Shadows. A field may shift and roil, being covered in tall grass one moment, a muddy pit the next. Spectres and Plasmics might roam, and sudden Nihils fissure open. There just isn't enough emotional investment or psychic weight to &amp;quot;stabilize&amp;quot; those areas. Most uninhabited areas are reflective of their Skinlands counterparts, but more representative than analogous. So a forest in the Shadowlands may occupy the same space as a forest in the Skinlands, but not every tree will share the exact same placement (and the Shadowlands forest will vary in appearance and mood depending on what the Wraiths expect).<br /> <br /> Necropoli are more like islands in a calm sea rather than a storm, so calm that it's often mistaken for land. A Maelstrom will quickly disabuse anyone of that notion, though.<br /> <br /> It's not that Wraiths weren't able to access places like the Somme, but that the Somme wasn't<i> the Somme</i> until it was <b>the Somme</b>, if that makes sense, like Verdun was just some hills until it was <b>Verdun</b>, and the beaches at Normandy were just a place where sand met water until D-Day. The geographical features and emotional resonances weren't &amp;quot;locked in&amp;quot; until those events happened.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing to forgive (pun intended) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Although my views are a little different I love the evocative imagery of your descriptions.<br /> <br /> I'm going to have to side with Nazfool on this one.<br /> I think a combination of the two is a nice equilibrium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T04:14:38-07:00","id":907562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907436#post907436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><sup>\u2020(If this were the <i>Vampire</i> forums, I'm sure the first response would be something like &amp;quot;You can't use the fiction to answer a question!&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></sup></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you kinda can't...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:13:12-07:00","id":907667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907436#post907436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <sup>\u2020(If this were the <i>Vampire</i> forums, I'm sure the first response would be something like &quot;You can't use the fiction to answer a question!&quot;)</sup></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">From what I understand, VtM has some fiction that irritatingly goes against the grain of RAW. I don\u2019t read VtM fiction, but the short of it seems to be that the fiction-fluff doesn\u2019t match up with the game-crunch.<br /> <br /> The WtO topic of discussion lacks definable crunch so, IMO,using the fiction-fluff as inspiration is appropriate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:40:49-07:00","id":907764,"title":"","content":"Nothing you are one of the Authors in WtO20?!<br /> <br /> Well it sure worked wonders for Exalted when they cut out all the excess Underworld and followed Wraiths Tempest as the default template. So it just sounds like the Wilderness is Maelstrom Tossed compared to Necropoli, and when the final Maelstrom hit it just enveloped Necropoli as well? So does that make Byways naturally fall on Areas that have been rivers or pathways at one point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T00:41:08-07:00","id":910610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=907764#post907764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing you are one of the Authors in WtO20?!</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish, but no.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:52:32-07:00","id":911942,"title":"","content":"Thing is, everything in the Underworld is based on emotion AND memory. I think this is kinda what <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing\">nothing</a></b> is getting at. That is, the old orchard where you used to play and whatnot WOULD be in the Shadowlands, but proper <i>wilderness</i> \u2013 as the OP specifically asked about \u2013 would not likely appear at all in the Shadowlands. This may pose issues with those of us who believe that the Shadowlands and the Skinlands are a one-to-one image of each other. The fact of the matter is that they are not such.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair, *I* do take a pretty narrow definition of what constitutes 'wilderness' being places not used much by anyone, and that includes such 'obvious' things as widely visible mountain ranges, long stretches of otherwise empty highway, and the 'stuff' that's all inbetween here and there are wilderness. Those things just don't exist in the Shadowlands 'coz no one cares enough about their memories of them to conjure a reflection. The Shadowlands are close to the Skinlands in many ways, and the most notable is how the thoughts and feels of the living sculpt the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> On some level it's possible that the dead could sculpt their reflection of our world, true. However, this becomes difficult when one factors in how brief most wraiths' stay in the Shadowlands is. As fetters are lost, sheer Passion cannot keep one of the restless dead from falling into the Tempest. There ARE some few who do so, but they do not have the power to keep things in the Shadowlands like living humanity does.<br /> <br /> ...This is borne out by 'the RULEZ' in passages that say travel between necropoli mus be made via the Tempest or other means. A ghost cannot 'walk' from Denver to Miami and then 'swim' to Bristol. Yeah, there's SOME contradictory evidence to this (in books like <i>Blood-dimmed Tides</i> and in one of the <b>Werewolf: the Wyld West</b> titles, I think), but the rules as written don't allow for proper wilderness in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> As ever, mileage varies, and I'm all for weirdness that contradicts whatever *I* think is 'canon' in a game. The above is more my own take on it than anything else, and know that I DO appreciate this conversation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T22:18:50-07:00","id":912098,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar409_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"409\" data-vbnamecard=\"409\">Phaolan</a> that's pretty much what I'm trying to say. I'm guess I'm just not articulating myself correctly. Like, if a wraith is walking from Desert Town A to Desert Town B, and no <b>events</b> happened in the Skinlands to give the route emotional/psychic definition, it's just going to be &quot;generic desert&quot; - sand and rocks, maybe a mountain range in the distance that never seems to move. But if a murder occurred at a gas station along the way, that and the surrounding area will appear in the Sahdowlands. And if there's a Nihill nearby, the landscape will be more chaotic and subject to change, like the Tempest &quot;leaking&quot; into the Shadowlands. Maybe the best way to put it would be that wilderness areas are &quot;closer&quot; to the edge of the Shadowlands that border the Tempest than Necropoli, like<br /> <br /> Skinlands<br /> Shadowlands<br /> (Necropoli)<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> (Wilderness)<br /> Tempest<br /> Labyrinth<br /> Oblivion<br /> <br /> So they're firmly in the Shadowlands, but they &quot;brush up&quot; against the membrane separating the Shadowlands from the Tempest, become a little &quot;influenced&quot; by the Sea of Shadows. Like the above example, a wraith traveling this &quot;limbo desert&quot; comes across some watering hole, then uh oh! They've stumbled into the Dark Kingdom of Flint and now they're fucked.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> (I was a little tired the first time, and I'm a little drunk this time, so please forgive me if I offend.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:52:11-07:00","id":912312,"title":"","content":"Sorry, guys, it seems like the intrinsic rules of Wraith don't back this up. The Skinlands ARE. That's what the Rule of Ouch is all about. You can't possibly be saying that every tree a wraith avoids walking through is a tree that was DEEPLY, TRULY cared for, every parking structure was utterly meaningful, etc.. They are THERE and the wraiths much deal with them. A city isn't some weird mashed up psychotropic salad where the downtown is larger and more full of structures cheek-by-jowl and the McMansion suburbs are squished up tiny little places because of their lack of meaning. Psychic imprint doesn't fold or stretch or compact or negate space, it just effects how present said material will be in the Shadowlands when its Skinlands tenure is done. The land doesn't have to be a sous-Relic to be there. It's THERE. Sure, that downtown is FULL of stuff. It's full of all the things that are there in the Skinlands jostling with and overlapping with the memories of the past buildings people did care about and the structures wraiths have built from the detritus of fading memories and jury-rigged together. That's another reason Haunts rock. Skinland architecture/geography and that of the Shadowlands are definitely sympathetic if not actually congruent. <br /> <br /> Because the Shadowlands are reflection of the Skinlands until you start going &quot;that-a-way&quot; off the map to where-there-be-Tempest and cities built of memories. The &quot;land shaped by passion&quot; is out there. Sure, Stygia might be squishy and shaped by passion more than geography, but, like Swar, the Dark Kingdom of Sand, the Far Shores, et al. it's because in essence it's more of an idea of a place than a place. Sorta a shaped part of the Tempest. Effectively, Stygia, accessible via Byways and Tempest, is the nearest of the Far Shores.<br /> <br /> Besides, even if I did buy into this &quot;passion&quot; = &quot;space&quot; idea, doesn't a farmer care about his fields? In a fundamental way that is more visceral than, say, people care about a shed behind their house? Or the entire area a trapper uses for his lines? The area over which a hunter ranges to catch his prey? Doesn't the sea matter DEEPLY to the fisherman? The road to the traveler? How many people have to care before something becomes &quot;real enough&quot;? After all, it just takes ONE wraith to make multiple things into Fetters.<br /> <br /> I would by that the Tempest may be a little &quot;closer&quot; in places where there are less people. But it seems just as likely that it's the opposite. Nihils happen where bad things happen to people. Where there are few people, fewer bad things can happen to them and there would be less Nihils. Also, it seems to take increased population to generate Maelstroms more frequently (particularly since a lot of Maelstroms, Great and otherwise are just massive examples of Nihil production. Ruptures due to bad things happening to people as opposed to pin-pricks). Maybe the Wilderness is MORE solid and dependable. But there are less Haunts when things do get bad. (Nasty emotional weather downwind from those memory and deed choked cities). And there is very little Pathos out there to keep a wraith going. Fetters are far away and Slumber isn't going to be an option. And, if anything bad does happen, it's off to the Tempest and back to your Fetters which are probably back where there are people, etc. Wilderness isn't absent, it's just so painfully, desperately <i><b>empty</b></i>....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-11-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:03:35-07:00","id":912501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=912312#post912312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, guys, it seems like the intrinsic rules of Wraith don't back this up. The Skinlands ARE.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two are not mutually exclusive, it turns out. A wraith who would need to manifest in the Skinlands to travel beyond a Necropolis, and THAT is where the so-called 'rule out ouch' would come up. However, this does NOT mean that self-same ghost can walk anywhere <i>within</i> the Shadowlands... Since the metaphysics of what makes anything there real (for want of a better word) is based on the combination of memory and emotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=912312#post912312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A city isn't some weird mashed up psychotropic salad where the downtown is larger and more full of structures cheek-by-jowl and the McMansion suburbs are squished up tiny little places because of their lack of meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a matter of fact, it kinda is, I think. That is, the older and more remembered parts of any city remain real no matter what. Old neighborhoods that were wiped out to make away for new buildings remain in the Shadowlands long after they're mostly forgotten in the Skinlands. New suburbs take a while to 'get established' around a Necropolis, and a 'McMansion' that has traded hands four or five times in a few years isn't guaranteed to show up in the Necropolis. Of course, if there was an ugly foreclosure or some tragedy that caused those exchanges, well THAT is what the Underworld is all about. There's that great example of the Brown Derby in Los Angeles, you know that was torn down, paved over, and then a NEW Brown Derby opened right next to it? Turns out, enough people remember and care about the old place that BOTH stand side-by-side in the Shadowlands, though one is a parking lot in the Skinlands. Yeah, it's in the core book if you wanna look it up.<br /> <br /> Your example of a farmer's fields may or may not work out the way you describe, but it's that <i>maybe</i> part that I don't want to get hung up on. A farmstead that a family ran for decades or centuries, sure it's all gonna pop up in the Shadowlands. An industrial farm run by a heartless corporation where the workers are merely wage slaves growing maize or tulips or poppies? That's not the same thing. Just because someone saw it, took a picture, and then maybe remembers it does not guarantee a place in the Underworld. For my buck, that's why I find the Shadowlands such a terrifying concept. Nothing here is guaranteed to cross over.<br /> <br /> Memory of the living is what the Shadowlands is built on, but the memories of the dead are what make a city like Stygia possible. The buildings on the island are all those that have been forgotten by the quick, and they now only exist in the Tempest.<br /> <br /> ...But again, I'm not gonna say that at your version need match mine. I actually do like that notion of the desperate emptiness, by the bye, so we're not impossibly far apart in our views. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T08:27:37-07:00","id":912811,"title":"","content":"I still don't buy it. That's not what has been explicitly stated in the rules, in the supplements, etc. . Things in the Skinlands and Shadowlands are overlapping. You don't have the memory of historic building X in this location, then, when it is demolished and replaced with a parking lot, the memory of building X sorta 'moves aside&quot; and now is next to empty Skinlands space that is the parking lot. They are on top of each other. The Shadowlands echo of the building is standing in the middle of the new empty parking lot. Living people are walking through it's walls. Wraiths are standing on floors that are effectively in &quot;mid-air&quot; to the Quick getting into and out of their cars. The walls of Building X are opaque to any vision that looks into the Shadowlands, so only the wraiths at the windows are visible. Etc. It's not the wraiths in Building X looking down on the parking lot from &quot;next door&quot;. <br /> <br /> Using your version, Lifesight wouldn't really work all that well. It would be a non-Euclidean nightmare and really impossible to describe. The Shadowlands version of a city would be MUCH larger too. That's never been indicated. That's not the Atlanta described in Necropolis Atlanta at all.<br /> <br /> Hell, there would BE no Great War. Wraiths couldn't get to the battlefields because they were &quot;out in the Tempest&quot; since no one has ever cared enough about that patch of ground in the woods. Except for a few treasured cottages, which would be right next to each other. The actual battles in the forests and fields would be &quot;lost&quot; in the space that is squeezed out of existence because of it's lack of any emotional weight. That's not the setting described in the Great War book at all. And, no, the fact that they sites will gain more &quot;psychic reality&quot; because of the battledin your system bears no weight. Wraiths wouldn't be able to get to the battle until it was over? Or it would &quot;pop&quot; into existence the second that the fighting started? That's not how the adventure described works. Wouldn't it mean that EVERY sight were a battle took place would be reflected? A world of empty battlefields located right next to each other and to cities with all the space in between &quot;deleted&quot;?<br /> <br /> There seems to be a lot of attribution of the idea of how emotional investment can make things &quot;real&quot; or &quot;more real&quot; in the Shadowlands and the actual geographically mechanics of the Shadowlands. The lands of the Dead are to the lands of the Quick in the Dark Umbra are equivalent to the Middle Umbra Periphery and lands of the spirits. (That's flat out been stated.) Sure, there is &quot;another&quot; direction, sorta &quot;out there&quot;, that can be traversed along Byways and more than one &quot;place&quot; can be adjacent. Wraiths can dig in the ground and make a pit or they can use Arcanoi to punch a Nihil in the same ground, the two are both &quot;holes&quot; but they are very different in character; the sky is the &quot;grey above&quot; but, if you build a makeshift &quot;Tower of Babel&quot; to get to the Tempest, you might not get there, you might just get a tall tower (but it will get blown down by the high winds and the boundary between the air and the Tempest is as thin as it is between the water and the Tempest, so you just might be able to build a tower to the Tempest. Or not. It will depend, probably on the intent of the builders and the vicissitudes of Oblivion), There are even places where the Shadowlands are getting or have been sorta &quot;squeezed&quot; by the weight of emotion and location may be &quot;budding&quot; off into the Tempest as new &quot;detached&quot; realms that are more like the Far Shores than they are like the geographically expanse of Dark Kingdoms of Iron or Jade in the Shadowlands proper. You can walk the Shadowlands of Egypt forever and stay in the Dark Kingdom of Iron, though you are much closer to the the Dark Kingdom of Sand than you would be anywhere else. Duat is &quot;right there&quot;. It's &quot;next door&quot; in a way that has nothing to do with three dimensions. But it's not here and here is not there. That's one of the reasons traveling the &quot;wilderness&quot; between necropoli in North America can be problematic. The &quot;empty spaces&quot; are Dark Kingdom of Flint and Obsidian &quot;adjacent&quot; and the wraiths there are not in a forgiving frame of mind... nor are the many many many specters left after the despair of genocide, displacement and disease. It's not that you can't get from Albuquerque to Santa Fe by walking down the highway. It's more like the route is decidedly not safe. Take a train. Those are also along Byways, so here and there might even be closer and a speedier journey overall and the option to go places that aren't really on the map. &quot;Next stop, Stygia&quot;. Or go in a Relic stagecoach, station wagon or caddy on a roadtrip along the Quick highway, but take a lot of firepower.<br /> <br /> You can go ahead and use your version. Golden Rule and all. But I don't think that it's really applicable in pretty much any of the Shadowlands as stated in the rules. Effectively, your Shadowlands are ALL the Tempest. It's all perspective nightmare of Dali-esque and Bosch-ian phantasmagorical landscapes. And if that's everyday, then who needs the Tempest at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T11:59:12-07:00","id":912907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=912811#post912811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can go ahead and use your version. Golden Rule and all. But I don't think that it's really applicable in pretty much any of the Shadowlands as stated in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, looking back at the rules, I'm not so sure of my own approach, it turns out. A lot of my view is based on what others would consider 'fluff' and even fiction, but it ALSO is a form of how I interpret the nature of the Shadowlands. It turns out that the rules DO say that the Shadowlands are a full reflection of our world (i.e. the Skinlands), but the incredible focus on necropoli and the straight up confusing nature of how the geography of the Underworld is presented in the core (Second Edition) <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> doesn't make me feel that the 'canon' is an perfectly accurate or precise source...<br /> <br /> I choose atmosphere over rules, sure, but on the other hand, your statement about how dangerous the 'inbetween' spaces are makes it kinda moot as to whether there's proper wilderness in the Shadowlands. By that I mean, if it's there, who's to know? Only an insane ghost would go exploring there. Thanks for setting me straight on this, I guess. Cheers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:48:03-07:00","id":913410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=912907#post912907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, looking back at the rules, I'm not so sure of my own approach, it turns out. A lot of my view is based on what others would consider 'fluff' and even fiction, but it ALSO is a form of how I interpret the nature of the Shadowlands. It turns out that the rules DO say that the Shadowlands are a full reflection of our world (i.e. the Skinlands), but the incredible focus on necropoli and the straight up confusing nature of how the geography of the Underworld is presented in the core (Second Edition) <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> doesn't make me feel that the 'canon' is an perfectly accurate or precise source...<br /> <br /> I choose atmosphere over rules, sure, but on the other hand, your statement about how dangerous the 'inbetween' spaces are makes it kinda moot as to whether there's proper wilderness in the Shadowlands. By that I mean, if it's there, who's to know? Only an insane ghost would go exploring there. Thanks for setting me straight on this, I guess. Cheers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, do it your own way. There are definitely some stories in the WtO fiction that &quot;get it wrong&quot;, but, probably, on the whole, less so than the corpus of fiction for the other games. Or maybe not. I do remember reading some WtO fiction that seemed to nail the setting and some that were atmospheric but were pretty loose with one aspect or the other and others that should have been in some book of ghost stories that had nothing to do with WtO.<br /> <br /> The Wilderness might have some VERY interesting spots. Battlefields, forgotten, dimly or well-remembered, can easily be away from any necropolis associated with a modern city (also, think abandoned cities, a la the ghost towns in the supplement of the same name). And they have a decent chance of being Fetters too, so casualties may be popping up there after surviving Harrowings. It even brings to mind the concept of sua-necropoli outside of a Skinlands city due to the importance of the place to those who died there. There's not much infrastructure at Gettysburgh, but there could very easily be a Necropolis there. Anyplace where there is a lot of emotion going on. Burning Man would be a FEAST of Pathos for the right wraiths (and changelings too). Just Puppetry there, ride a Fetter (make one with Lifeweb), Inhabit pretty much anything going there... Hell, the right wraith and a Ren Faire. You could easily have a travelling wraith game that would work. There are lots of different &quot;islands&quot; out there in the empty spaces. From the beloved family farm home Haunt to the aforementioned battlefields, to the echoes of the weirdness associated with &quot;legendary&quot; roads lined with &quot;attractions&quot; that once attracted the Pathos of travelers (a la Route 66), to necropoli large and small, etc. And a lot of VERY BAD THINGS have happened on the roads, in the empty spaces (perhaps made empty by such fell deeds) that could easily be Nihils or even Specter Hives (and what is the Hierarchy doing about them?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:50:18-07:00","id":991212,"title":"","content":"I much prefer Phaolan and nothing's take on &quot;the spaces between,&quot; myself. As Phaolan said: &quot;atmosphere over rules,&quot; especially since we're talking about make-believe ghost people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson","name":"LordCrimson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:48:16-07:00","id":991448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=991212#post991212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I much prefer Phaolan and nothing's take on &quot;the spaces between,&quot; myself. As Phaolan said: &quot;atmosphere over rules,&quot; especially since we're talking about make-believe ghost people.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do it that way, if you so choose. It's not canon, so you are Golden Ruling your setting. It might a significant departure or it might not matter much, depending on what your story is and what your characters do.<br /> <br /> There are some consequences to that choice. You've effectively removed Wraiths from having to interact with the Quicklands. It's a lot like Changelings with Freeholds and the Dreaming. but that's where the entire game takes place. It would be like having vampires have havens that exist in places that don't exist for mortals. It makes enforcing the Dictum Mortuum VERY easy. Wraiths should stay in the &quot;Ghost-Town&quot; and anyone hanging out in places that match up to the living world are going to be immediately suspect. Especially since travel between these in-between places can be by Argos and not by walking from &quot;here&quot; to &quot;there&quot; via a street that living people frequent. A lot of &quot;Show me your pass!&quot; or get forged. And that's just one example...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:16:36-07:00","id":991578,"title":"","content":"I tend to deviate from the standard rules by allowing animal Wraiths, similar to the ones found in the African Shadowlands, to exist within all Shadowlands. For example, outside of the Shadowlands cities in the USA, Animal Wraiths of bears, cougars, and wolves hunt down American Wraiths because they are not protected by the ancient treaties signed by the Native American Wraiths. It makes Wraith players much more paranoid about walking from one mortal town to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:03:10-07:00","id":991604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=991578#post991578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to deviate from the standard rules by allowing animal Wraiths, similar to the ones found in the African Shadowlands, to exist within all Shadowlands. For example, outside of the Shadowlands cities in the USA, Animal Wraiths of bears, cougars, and wolves hunt down American Wraiths because they are not protected by the ancient treaties signed by the Native American Wraiths. It makes Wraith players much more paranoid about walking from one mortal town to another.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I've done something similar, except I use &quot;wild plasmics.&quot; Just like it sounds, these are plasmic critters (that may or may not resemble living animals) that roam the Shadowlands. I was originally inspired by a late night TNT binge of <i>Critters</i> followed by <i>Langoliers</i>. Nowadays, I think <i>Stranger Things</i> would be fair inspiration. Anyhoo, I like the animal-wraith idea.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","user":"Nazfool","date":". 10-23-2016, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:37:48-07:00","id":991619,"title":"","content":"I cannot really take credit for it, animal ghost stories are as common as human ghost stories, and I was really disappointed when I did not see Animal Wraiths anywhere except for the African Shadowlands. Animal Wraiths are not created from the memories of individual animals but, instead, are created from the memories of multiple animals. Of course, modern factory farming methods mean that there are a lot of traumatized animals to make Animal Wraiths, though I think that extremely traumatized animals would probably be too unstable to contribute to Animal Wraiths (though they may feed the creation of Animal Shadows).<br /> <br /> I have toyed with the idea of allowing Animal Wraith PCs, but I have never gone ahead and done it. I wonder, has anyone allowed Animal Wraith PCs? If so, would you be willing to share your experiences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:46:10-07:00","id":991879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=991578#post991578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to deviate from the standard rules by allowing animal Wraiths, similar to the ones found in the African Shadowlands, to exist within all Shadowlands. For example, outside of the Shadowlands cities in the USA, Animal Wraiths of bears, cougars, and wolves hunt down American Wraiths because they are not protected by the ancient treaties signed by the Native American Wraiths. It makes Wraith players much more paranoid about walking from one mortal town to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the wraiths raiding out of the Dark Kingdom of Flint specifically mentioned in the setting aren't dangerous enough? <br /> <br /> Overall, this really does cause a cluster of problems that might or might not need to deal with. Those don't sound like the ghosts of animals at all. They sound like spirits. Up to and including (probably especially) these &quot;contracts&quot; You're definitely crossing over two things White Wolf likes to sharply demarcate. There are consequences to the setting if you do this. Particularly if werewolves are an issue you might want to bring in.<br /> <br /> Moreover, why aren't there contracts with the between Western civilization and their animal ghosts? Lots of animals are really important in many of those cultures. Where are the pet dogs? Cats? (Though cats probably do their own thing after death) The scary and or important animals of those cultures? (Bears, wolves, lions, aurochs, swans, stags, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:50:11-07:00","id":991881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=991619#post991619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot really take credit for it, animal ghost stories are as common as human ghost stories, and I was really disappointed when I did not see Animal Wraiths anywhere except for the African Shadowlands. Animal Wraiths are not created from the memories of individual animals but, instead, are created from the memories of multiple animals. Of course, modern factory farming methods mean that there are a lot of traumatized animals to make Animal Wraiths, though I think that extremely traumatized animals would probably be too unstable to contribute to Animal Wraiths (though they may feed the creation of Animal Shadows).<br /> <br /> I have toyed with the idea of allowing Animal Wraith PCs, but I have never gone ahead and done it. I wonder, has anyone allowed Animal Wraith PCs? If so, would you be willing to share your experiences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like Animal Specters. If you are creating wraiths from emotional trauma, then modern slaughterhouses, chicken farms, etc, wouldn't be something for a PC. They'd be something for a nightmare. An amalgam Mortwright that's a huge masses of feathers with chicken heads and claws with those dead velociraptor eyes. And if collective trauma is what brings them across then most animal ghosts are going to be really really bad things. Chain them down with soulsteel and hack chunks off to forge. <br /> <br /> And why don't masses of humans who all die experiencing emotional trauma all come across as amalgamated entities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:56:31-07:00","id":991909,"title":"","content":"You are projecting modern norms onto our ancestors. Western European culture has not traditionally valued animals when compared to Native American culture, so Animal Wraiths would be more antagonistic to Western Europeans than Native Americans. In the case of dogs and cats, Western Europeans (with exception of the upper class) really did not value dogs and cats beyond their utility until last century. While the average situation of pets have improved, and horses have transitioned from work animals to pets over the last fifty years, the average situation of farm animals have declined over the last fifty years, so there really is no reason for Animal Wraiths (with the exception of well-treated pets) to really like Human Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Humans have developed Psyches before they die, which is why they do not normally create amalgamated entities after death. Weak-willed humans become Drone and strong-willed humans become Wraiths or Specters. I imagine that animals do not have developed Psyches before they die, with the possible exception of Animal Kinfolk, so they have to amalgamate to form anything in the Dark Umbra, whether they form Animal Wraiths or Animal Specters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:28:04-07:00","id":993005,"title":"","content":"By the way, it's already implied in the setting that plasmics might be the remnants of less sentient creatures and/or half-dissolved human memories. Sea of Shadows speculated on the matter, and it makes sense (animals create flimsier psychic residues, so they can't coalesce into full wraiths, but they do shape plasmics in much the same way fleeting emotions create chimerae in Changeling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:01:46-07:00","id":993826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=991909#post991909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are projecting modern norms onto our ancestors. Western European culture has not traditionally valued animals when compared to Native American culture, so Animal Wraiths would be more antagonistic to Western Europeans than Native Americans. In the case of dogs and cats, Western Europeans (with exception of the upper class) really did not value dogs and cats beyond their utility until last century. While the average situation of pets have improved, and horses have transitioned from work animals to pets over the last fifty years, the average situation of farm animals have declined over the last fifty years, so there really is no reason for Animal Wraiths (with the exception of well-treated pets) to really like Human Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Humans have developed Psyches before they die, which is why they do not normally create amalgamated entities after death. Weak-willed humans become Drone and strong-willed humans become Wraiths or Specters. I imagine that animals do not have developed Psyches before they die, with the possible exception of Animal Kinfolk, so they have to amalgamate to form anything in the Dark Umbra, whether they form Animal Wraiths or Animal Specters.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually, you are projecting your ideas of Native American culture as delivered in a modern format to a modern audience and disregarding the validity of Western European culture and ideals which are also not a part of modern populist conceptions. The validity of the &quot;Native Americans respect/respected animals and Western Europeans don't/didn't&quot; is actually an indictment of the American (not European) conceptualization of the &quot;noble savage&quot;. Animals mean different things to different cultures and the players may change, but the basics don't. Except on a very basic level... If you said something like Native American cultures start with a different perception of animals from Europeans due to the fact that domestication followed very different courses.... That's fundamentally true, though, strictly speaking complete or useful.<br /> <br /> To take this down the level that White Wolf operates... Witness the fact that Werewolf has NO problem coming up many many many &quot;totems&quot; for the European tribes that are fundamentally mythologically just as sound as anything for the Pure Lands tribes. (Or, all too often, both groups of totems have pretty much nothing to do with anything relevant... they just sounded cool. Oh...and look, there's that &quot;noble savage&quot; idea rearing it's head again with that whole &quot;Pure&quot; Lands conceptualization.) <br /> <br /> Dansky et al. made a very definitive point about the lack of animal ghosts (except in Africa, which is noted as particularly the exception to the rule). There seems to be something fundamental in what wraiths actually ARE that had them drawing a bright line between whatever it is that human consciousness is and how it persists after death and with that of animals, even though that's become something that is more and more difficult to determine for scientists who study the meaning of &quot;consciousness&quot;, &quot;intelligence&quot;, &quot;theory of mind&quot;, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:14:22-07:00","id":993957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=993826#post993826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, actually, you are projecting your ideas of Native American culture as delivered in a modern format to a modern audience and disregarding the validity of Western European culture and ideals which are also not a part of modern populist conceptions. The validity of the &amp;quot;Native Americans respect/respected animals and Western Europeans don't/didn't&amp;quot; is actually an indictment of the American (not European) conceptualization of the &amp;quot;noble savage&amp;quot;. Animals mean different things to different cultures and the players may change, but the basics don't. Except on a very basic level... If you said something like Native American cultures start with a different perception of animals from Europeans due to the fact that domestication followed very different courses.... That's fundamentally true, though, strictly speaking complete or useful.<br /> <br /> To take this down the level that White Wolf operates... Witness the fact that Werewolf has NO problem coming up many many many &amp;quot;totems&amp;quot; for the European tribes that are fundamentally mythologically just as sound as anything for the Pure Lands tribes. (Or, all too often, both groups of totems have pretty much nothing to do with anything relevant... they just sounded cool. Oh...and look, there's that &amp;quot;noble savage&amp;quot; idea rearing it's head again with that whole &amp;quot;Pure&amp;quot; Lands conceptualization.) <br /> <br /> Dansky et al. made a very definitive point about the lack of animal ghosts (except in Africa, which is noted as particularly the exception to the rule). There seems to be something fundamental in what wraiths actually ARE that had them drawing a bright line between whatever it is that human consciousness is and how it persists after death and with that of animals, even though that's become something that is more and more difficult to determine for scientists who study the meaning of &amp;quot;consciousness&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;intelligence&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;theory of mind&amp;quot;, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it always occurred to me that the 'animal' wraiths of the Bush of Ghosts were little more than moliated human wraiths. Their presence was intentionally conspicuous, which in the World of Darkness usually means something sinister (in the same way Swar looks like a paradise but is actually a Malfean feasting on the Indian dead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:20:04-07:00","id":993958,"title":"","content":"Another theory: the animal wraiths of the Bush of Ghosts could be a unique kind of spectre or drone, either in disguise or warped by cultural attitudes/oppression/poor self-image (they were treated as less than human in life, so they became less than human in death, or they had a poor sense of self so are unable to take on human form, etc). They could be sentinels and guards. Or they could be servants of some beastly Malfean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:18:00-07:00","id":994145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/907001-shadowlands-and-the-wilderness?p=993958#post993958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another theory: the animal wraiths of the Bush of Ghosts could be a unique kind of spectre or drone, either in disguise or warped by cultural attitudes/oppression/poor self-image (they were treated as less than human in life, so they became less than human in death, or they had a poor sense of self so are unable to take on human form, etc). They could be sentinels and guards. Or they could be servants of some beastly Malfean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, to combine this post with your previous one, there is something about the Bush of Ghosts that keeps animal ghosts from degenerating into plasmics... (Though, TBH, many of the plasmics depicted so far give me more of a Burgess Shale/Cthulhu feel than that of a &quot;melted cat&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}